# Security headers, applied to every path the site serves (pages, JS,
# CSS, images). Deployed by the workflow and the manual recipe, which
# both copy this file into the staging root, so it must sit at the repo
# root beside index.html.
#
# CSP: everything is same-origin except three allow-listed things ·
# Google Fonts (the linked style sheet, then the font files it pulls),
# and the public donations ledger API the wall reads and the give form
# posts to. The single hash in script-src pins the page's one inline
# block (the cover bootstrap at the top of index.html); every other
# script loads from js/. blob: covers the give form's compressed
# receipt preview; data: covers the SVG glyphs inlined in styles.css.
# frame-ancestors 'none' plus X-Frame-Options DENY means no other site
# can frame this page.
#
# When the inline script in index.html changes, its hash changes with
# it: recompute with
#   node -e "const fs=require('fs'),c=require('crypto');const
#   html=fs.readFileSync('index.html','utf8');const
#   re=/<script>([\s\S]*?)<\/script>/g;let m;while((m=re.exec(html))){
#   console.log('sha256-'+c.createHash('sha256').update(m[1]).digest('base64'))}"
# and paste the new value into script-src below, or the cover bootstrap
# will be blocked and first-paint animation states will miss.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'sha256-/+xqIBcUmh558CgcmY23cUC043KbwjfqvdeULhbIbOI='; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob:; connect-src 'self' https://bibleonline.pages.dev; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=()
